  "answer": "Windows Terminal already supports this, so no new option is needed. Set the profile's colorScheme to a light/dark pair, for example `\"colorScheme\": {\"light\": \"One Half Light\", \"dark\": \"One Half Dark\"}`. In the UI, this is under Profiles > Appearance > Color scheme. Put it in `profiles.defaults` to apply it to every profile. Also set the app's `theme` to `default` (\"Use Windows theme\"), not a fixed light or dark theme. The color scheme follows the app theme, so a fixed theme keeps it on one scheme. This is tracked in terminal#4066, and terminal#6491 and terminal#19560 were closed as duplicates of it. Switching by time of day (sunrise/sunset) isn't built in. It works if Windows switches its own theme on a schedule, for example with Night Light or the Auto Dark Mode tool."
